    "media:imagetext": "January 30, 1933.\nDear Debby\nThis aeries two of my shot gun correspondence being broadcast\nfrom somewhere on the storm tossed so called Pacific Ocean. We sailed from\nVictoria at five thirty Saturday afternoon, and after passing through the\nstraits headed out across the Paoifio. We immediately ran into what the Cap-\ntain calls \" a bit of nasty weather \" which has put most of the few passengers\nin their respective staterooms. Saturday night there were only three men who\nshowed up for dinner besides Groeger and meself. Groeger is an old sailing\nship captain so the thick weather bothers him not at all. So far it has not\neffected me and I am hoping that I will turn out to be a good sailor - I have\nreally never been in rough weather before as my very limited experience has\nall been in fair weather. The ship is rolling and plunging so that it is ex-\nremely hard to get around. Outaide the oold spray is flying the whole length\nof the ship and the rigging is loe covered. There are no games on deok and\nno steamer chairs. The few passengers who venture out of their rooms sit\naround the open fires in the \"tap room\" and work on their \"seotch and Soda\".\nYesterday, Sunday, Groeger and I called on the Captain and made arrangements\nfor Groeger to have access to the bridge and chart room so that he can make\nthe weather obversations which he was instructed to secure. The Captain is an\nEnglishman who has sailed all over the World during his thirty years at sea,\nand he seems to enjoy swapping yarns with Groeger and giving information on\nflying conditions. He is very much ammused at the idea of ever flying across\nthe Pacific and of course knows nothing whatever about airtransportation or\nits limitations. Lest night we had a Movie, Careless Age, featuring Douglas\nFairbanke and Loreta Young. It was an old \"talkie\" with no talking. The girls\n• wore dresses which came just to the lees and looked awfully funny. After each\nreel a sign came on \"ONE MOMENT PLEASE\" and the Chink who was the operator\nwould put on the next reel. All the crew except the officers are Chinese and\nnone of them can underatand English. My stateroom steward looks like \u0026 Guinea\nPig and so I call him \"G P\". He gives me a lot of service as he has no one else\nto look after. This morning Groeger and I took \"shots\" for Typhold and Friday",
